                                                              "summary":  "Damodaran examines how rising US Treasury rates in 2026 ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â with 10-year yields reaching 4.75% by August ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â affect bonds and stocks differently. Bond prices have declined in line with higher discount rates, but equity markets have held steady because corporate earnings have risen enough to offset the valuation drag. He argues that interest rate movements are fundamentally driven by inflation expectations and real GDP growth, not Fed policy, and that investors who obsess over Fed decisions are looking at the wrong variable.",
