                                                              "summary":  "Damodaran argues that venture capitalists systematically prioritize revenue scaling over profitability, creating misaligned incentives throughout the startup ecosystem. He demonstrates that while a small subset of businesses can simultaneously scale and profit, most cannot, yet continue attracting capital on growth metrics alone. Changes in private and public capital markets have deepened this tilt, resulting in companies carrying sky-high valuations built on business models that may never achieve sustainable economics.",
